   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I want to create a matrix mix[2,Q] in parameters with an idea that</div><div>mix[,1] is 2-simplex, mix[,2] is 2-simplex,...., mix[,Q] is 2-simplex.</div><div><br></div><div>To do this, i&#39;ve written the script below :</div><div><br></div><div>parameters{</div><div>         <font color=\"#ff0000\"> simplex[2*Q] all_mix</font>;</div><div>}</div><div><br></div><div>transformed parameters{</div><div>          real mix[2,Q];</div><div>          for(q in 1:Q){</div><div>                  for(i in 1:2){</div><div>                         mix[i,q] &lt;- all_mix[2*(q-1)+p];</div><div>                  }</div><div>          }</div><div>}</div><div><br></div><div>My question is i&#39;m not sure to write what i want to obtain.</div><div>Indeed, I believe that defining : </div><div>           <font color=\"#ff0000\">simplex[2*Q] all_mix</font></div><div>           </div><div>implies that the sum of matrix equals 1, but not that each sum of the matrix columns equals 1. Yet, my aim is that each sum of the columns of the matrix equals 1... </div><div><br></div><div>Could you help me, please ?</div><div>Bests regards</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "igKNozkc4_EJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2015-04-02T17:15:21Z",
   "subject": "Re: Simplex Matrix",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Thursday, April 2, 2015 at 10:51:56 AM UTC-4, Eric Innocents EBOULET wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Indeed, I believe that defining : <div>           <font color=\"#ff0000\">simplex[2*Q] all_mix</font></div><div>           </div><div>implies that the sum of matrix equals 1, but not that each sum of the matrix columns equals 1. Yet, my aim is that each sum of the columns of the matrix equals 1... </div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>It is pretty easy if you generalize your conceptualization of a matrix to be a collection of Q vectors on a J-simplex. So in general you could do<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">simplex</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>and access the q-th simplex vector by<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">mix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span></div></code></div><br>But in the case that J = 2, you could also do<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mix_1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>transformed parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  mix </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> app</span><span style=\"color:#000\">end_col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mix_1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mix_1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Ben<br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
