     3,
     "<div><br><br>Le jeudi 2 avril 2015 19:15:21 UTC+2, Ben Goodrich a écrit :<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Thursday, April 2, 2015 at 10:51:56 AM UTC-4, Eric Innocents EBOULET wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Indeed, I believe that defining : <div>           <font color=\"#ff0000\">simplex[2*Q] all_mix</font></div><div>           </div><div>implies that the sum of matrix equals 1, but not that each sum of the matrix columns equals 1. Yet, my aim is that each sum of the columns of the matrix equals 1... </div></div></blockquote><div><br>It is pretty easy if you generalize your conceptualization of a matrix to be a collection of Q vectors on a J-simplex. So in general you could do<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">simplex</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>and access the q-th simplex vector by<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">mix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span></div></code></div><br>But in the case that J = 2, you could also do<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mix_1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>transformed parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  mix </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> app</span><span style=\"color:#000\">end_col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mix_1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mix_1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Ben<br></div></div></blockquote></div>"
